{"created": "2021-12-28T15:51:20.151590+00:00", "modified": "2024-09-28T19:55:21.348142+00:00", "id": 5807719, "conceptrecid": "5807718", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.5807719", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.5807718", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.5807719", "metadata": {"title": "Highly curated hERG dataset of 8879 unique molecular compounds with corresponding potency values", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.5807719", "publication_date": "2021-11-28", "description": "<p>This dataset was built during a research project, in the field of Computer-Aided Drug Discovery (CADD),&nbsp;funded by&nbsp;the Natural Sciences and Engineering Research Council of Canada (NSERC) Discovery grant. The aim of the project was to build&nbsp;descriptor-based machine learning models for hERG cardiotoxicity liability predictions. The dataset includes a total of 8879&nbsp;unique molecular compounds gathered from&nbsp;ChEMBL and PubChem publicly available bioactivity databases, as well as from literature mining. The list&nbsp;is split into 2 sets, 8380 for training and 499 for testing. All molecular compounds are represented in their SMILE format with their corresponding&nbsp;PIC50 potency values.</p>\n<p>To access the full original&nbsp;work, please visit the following link:&nbsp;&nbsp;<a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2112.13467\">Manuscript</a></p>\n<p><strong>Note:</strong> Upon usage of this data, kindly cite the original manuscript describing the curation process:<br><br>Arab, Issar, and Khaled Barakat. \"ToxTree: descriptor-based machine learning models for both hERG and Nav1. 5 cardiotoxicity liability predictions.\"&nbsp;<em>arXiv preprint arXiv:2112.13467</em> (2021).</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>Refer to our latest manually curated and a much larger dataset here: <a href=\"../record/8359714\">link</a>&nbsp;</strong></p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Arab, Issar", "affiliation": "Technical University of Munich"}, {"name": "Barakat, Khaled", "affiliation": "University of Alberta"}], "keywords": ["hERG, Cardiotoxicity, Drug discovery, QSAR models, In silico screening, Machine Learning, Deep Learning"], "resource_type": {"title": "Dataset", "type": "dataset"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 0, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "5807718"}}]}}, "title": "Highly curated hERG dataset of 8879 unique molecular compounds with corresponding potency values", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/5807719", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/5807719", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/5807719?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.5807719", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.5807719", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.5807719", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/5807719/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/5807718", "parent_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/5807718", "parent_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.5807718", "parent_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.5807718", "self_iiif_manifest": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:5807719/manifest", "self_iiif_sequence": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:5807719/sequence/default", "files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/5807719/files", "media_files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/5807719/media-files", "archive": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/5807719/files-archive", "archive_media": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/5807719/media-files-archive", "latest": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/5807719/versions/latest", "latest_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/5807719/latest", "versions": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/5807719/versions", "draft": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/5807719/draft", "access_links": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/5807719/access/links", "access_grants": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/5807719/access/grants", "access_users": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/5807719/access/users", "acce